--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -250,12 +250,47 @@ lower-case fzf syntax (`ctrl-r`, `alt-f`, `f1`, …); the three keys must be
 distinct and must not be a reserved fzf event name (`enter`, `change`, …), or
 ccsession exits with an error instead of starting the picker.
 
+## Local Nix setup
+
+Run `cs` (also available as `ccsession`) for Codex sessions. The conversation
+preview is at the top, with five session rows above the fixed bottom search bar.
+Mode prompts have the same width; result counts occupy a separate line, and the
+panes adapt when the terminal resizes.
+
+Normal unquoted input searches IDs and labels fuzzily inside fzf. Double quotes
+add case-insensitive Go regular expressions over visible chat text: `"mizu"`
+finds chat containing mizu, and `"mizu|water"` matches either. Mixed input such as
+`"mizu" dply` requires the quoted chat match AND a fuzzy match for `dply` in an
+ID, title, or one chat word (for example, deployment). Each term may match a
+different message. Multiple quoted conditions are also ANDed. Regex patterns
+use message-text substring semantics; use anchors when needed.
+
+Ctrl-G keeps content search strict: plain input is a case-insensitive literal
+substring, including spaces and punctuation. Quoted terms are regex; any bare
+terms alongside them are literal, not fuzzy. Ctrl-F returns to normal search.
+`cs --exact -q QUERY` treats all query punctuation, including quotes, literally.
+Invalid quoted patterns clear the list and show an error. Query edits and mode
+changes cannot resume stale content results while a reload is pending.
+
+Preview matches use reverse video: regex matches and the full word matching a
+fuzzy chat term are highlighted. Active searches show a window around a matching
+message, and long bodies are clipped around the hit; normal previews show the
+latest messages. The default fzf color scheme is light; set
+`CCSESSION_FZF_SCHEME=dark` for a dark terminal.
+
+Codex rows show `Original` or `Fork`; forks also show their immediate source ID
+in the preview and resume their own session. `Unknown` means the rollout header
+is unavailable. Subagent sessions are excluded, including direct locator lookup.
+Codex's read-only SQLite projections supply metadata and previews; each list
+invocation reads at most 16 lines / 1 MiB of each candidate's rollout header to
+identify forks. Unquoted fuzzy typing stays in fzf without rereading transcripts.
+
 ## How it works
 
 1. `ccsession list` reads the selected backend (`~/.claude/projects/*/` by
    default, or `--source=opencode` / `--source=grok` / `--source=codex` /
    `--source=pi` / `--source=omp` / `--source=kiro` / `--source=cortex`) and prints one TSV row
-   per session (`id`, `locator`, `epoch`, relative time, cwd basename, label).
+   per session (`id`, `locator`, `epoch`, relative time, cwd basename, label, session type).
    `ccsession list --json --limit N` emits the same candidates as a JSON array
    for agent integrations.
 2. `fzf` consumes the TSV. The three key bindings swap fzf's matcher
